(* In a global world, we need to share date and time information clearly

SenseTalk has a number of features that let you control how date/time information is displayed, and how it is interpreted.
*)

put the time
set the clockFormat to 24
put the time
put -

put the date // by default, the date shows in an ambiguous format 
put the year of "08/11/26"
put -

put the centuryCutoff // controls how 2-digit years are interpreted
put the year of "8/11/36"
put the year of "8/11/37"

set the centuryCutoff to 46
put the year of "8/11/37"
put -

put the basic date
put the long common date
put -

set the dateLocale to "es_ES" // show month and weekday names in Spanish
put the basic date
put the long common date
put -

put the international date
put the international time
put -
